<table align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="govd_hr" style="border-collapse: collapse; padding: 5px;" width="100%"><tr class="govd_hr_inner"><td style="border-collapse: collapse; vertical-align: top;" valign="top" width="100%"><hr/></td></tr></table>
<h1 align="left" class="govd_header" style="font-size: 14px; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #0F0101; text-align: left; margin: 0 0 5px; padding: 0;"><a class="gd_anchor" id="link_3" name="link_3" style="text-decoration: none; color: #1D5782;">Breaking: Active Cyber Breaches Affecting Public Water Systems Demand Immediate Action.</a></h1>
<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="gd_combo_table" style="border-collapse: collapse;" width="100%">
<tr>
<td style="border-collapse: collapse; vertical-align: top;" valign="top">
<img align="left" alt="Cybersecurity" class="govd_template_image" height="140" hspace="7" src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/MEDEP/2026/08/14139209/cybersecurity_original.jfif" style="width: 241px; height: auto; float: left; border: 0px none;" width="241"/>
<p style="margin-bottom: 1.0em; color: #000000; font: 14px/1.5 arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">The US EPA, FBI, Cybersecurity &amp; Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA), and Water Information Sharing &amp; Analysis Center (WaterISAC) have held urgent briefings regarding <strong>active and on-going cybersecurity breaches at dozens of Public Water Systems (PWSs) in at least seven states across the U.S.</strong> The targeted PWSs range in size from small to large.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 1.0em; color: #000000; font: 14px/1.5 arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Many wastewater systems use similar technology as found in the drinking water sector. A common symptom of these breaches includes a loss of PLC connectivity with devices. These incidents all involve vulnerabilities related to PLCs, as described in the <a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Flinks-2.govdelivery.com%2FCL0%2Fhttps%3A%252F%252Fwww.ic3.gov%252FCSA%252F2026%252F260722.pdf%253Futm_medium%3Demail%2526utm_source%3Dgovdelivery%2F1%2F0101019faef2edac-3e92bc93-cf5c-4211-b881-4b32ea3acd8b-000000%2FmWkD1XTyVXy7YxvCQsyR61SmZK9JJOgrByTC70uvZYQ%3D452&amp;data=05%7C02%7CJudy.K.Bruenjes%40maine.gov%7C29f513ada2454265eb4e08deef06ae44%7C413fa8ab207d4b629bcdea1a8f2f864e%7C0%7C0%7C639211009155631389%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=LIiyk60tHQY6J5WYOaJrKFHezj3vYeVVvlUVOTzQqOg%3D&amp;reserved=0" rel="noopener" style="color: #3034E9;" target="_blank" title="Iranian-Affiliated Cyber Actors Exploit Programmable Logic Controllers Across US Critical Infrastructure Advisory">Iranian-Affiliated Cyber Actors Exploit Programmable Logic Controllers Across US Critical Infrastructure</a> advisory (PDF).</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 1.0em; color: #000000; font: 14px/1.5 arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">The Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) has information and guidance regarding malicious cyber actors targeting PLCs.</p>
<ul style="list-style-position: inside; font: 13px/1.5 Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">
<li style="color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;"><a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Flinks-2.govdelivery.com%2FCL0%2Fhttps%3A%252F%252Fcontent.govdelivery.com%252Fattachments%252FMEHHS%252F2026%252F08%252F03%252Ffile_attachments%252F3734507%252FMalicious%252520Cyber%252520Actors%252520Targeting%252520Water%252520Sector%252520Internet-Facing%252520PLCs.pdf%2F1%2F0101019fc92098b2-71da2f0c-b7d8-4e9f-92a0-fc375faa5de6-000000%2F444gmMF4TdglA9gs-hjSrEqujZNkz65us6scPhrXVrI%3D452&amp;data=05%7C02%7CJudy.K.Bruenjes%40maine.gov%7C9fa8a9ea6c534ce5a5d908def24f]]></content><link href="https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/MEDEP/bulletins/421a6b4"/><category term="Maine Agencies"/><category term="DEP"/><category term="role:environmental-land-use"/><category term="role:securities-financial"/><published>2026-08-06T14:32:50.106865+00:00</published></entry><entry><id>https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/MEDEP/bulletins/420fa43#c2bdd98e2e202891</id><title>Maine DEP Issues Air Quality Alert as Particle Pollution Levels Predicted to Escalate to Unhealthy Ranges</title><updated>2026-08-29T20:54:33.303538+00:00</updated><content type="CDATA"><![CDATA[<article>
